RISC3D test kit 26 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 24's results: leaving out TORCS's glHint changed nothing. Leaving
out mipmaps made the scenery sharper, but the car stayed plain yellow
and the trees striped. Arrays in buffers (kits 20 and 21) made no
difference either.

This kit's rol-3d (0.14) redraws your recording on the GPU several
times, each with one more thing changed, to find what the Pi's GPU
driver gets wrong:

  ReplayGPU      unchanged
  ReplayImm      TORCS's array drawing done as glBegin/glEnd instead
  ReplayNoPush   glPushClientAttrib/glPopClientAttrib done by rol-3d
  ReplayClamp    GL_CLAMP texture edges as GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE
  ReplaySized    TORCS's old-style texture formats as modern ones
  ReplayNoAlpha  no alpha test (trees will show grey boxes: expected)
  ReplayAll      all of those at once
  ReplaySoft     software, for comparison

It now writes PNG pictures (the PPMs got damaged on the way to me).

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing the old one (kit 25 is
    withdrawn: it tested buffers again, which you'd already done).
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.14-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240
    Nothing needs reloading or restarting.

